     "name": "Jack Johnson",
     "sub": "Boxer · 1878 – 1946"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "born",
   "text": "He was born in Galveston, Texas, in 1878, to parents who had been enslaved.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "1878",
    "sub": "born in Galveston, Texas"
   },
   "overlays": {
    "pin": {
     "label": "Galveston",
     "sub": "Texas"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "champ",
   "text": "In 1908, in Sydney, Australia, he beat Tommy Burns, and became the first Black heavyweight champion of the world.",
   "section": "story",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "portrait",
    "focus": [
     0.48,
     0.2
    ],
    "zoom": [
     1.0,
     1.06
    ],
    "anchor": [
     0.48,
     0.3
    ]
   },
   "overlays": {
    "stamp": "Sydney, 1908"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "hope",
   "text": "Many white Americans were furious. They called for a Great White Hope to take the title back.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Furious",
    "sub": "white America wants the title back"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "jeffries",
   "text": "On July 4, 1910, in Reno, former champion Jim Jeffries came out of retirement to fight him. Johnson won.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "fight",
    "crop": [
     0.05,
     0.0,
     0.95,
     1.0
    ],
    "caption": "Johnson and Jeffries, Reno, July 4, 1910"
   },
   "overlays": {
    "pin": {
     "label": "Reno",
     "sub": "Nevada"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "riots",
   "text": "That night, white mobs attacked Black Americans in cities across the country.",
   "section": "cost",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Race riots",
    "sub": "after the fight, 1910"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "mann",
   "text": "In 1913, an all-white jury convicted him under the Mann Act, over his relationships with white women.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "etta",
    "crop": [
     0.0,
     0.0,
     1.0,
     0.75
    ],
    "caption": "Johnson and his wife Etta, 1910"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "prison",
   "text": "He fled the country. In 1920, he came back and served about ten months in federal prison.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Prison",
    "sub": "Leavenworth, 1920"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "death",
   "text": "He died in a car crash in 1946.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "smile",
    "focus": [
     0.48,
     0.4
    ],
    "zoom": [
